<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gaudete (Steeleye Span)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1973</span><span class="sg-chain-h">a cappella recording, UK number 14</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gaudete, Gaudete (Boston Camerata, Joel Cohen)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1985</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording on A Renaissance Christmas</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gaudete (Pertti Neumann, Albion)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1986</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gaudete (Anúna, Omnis, with Eimear Quinn)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1996</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gaudete (Tenebrae, arranged by Karl Jenkins)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2004</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement with percussion and a cappella</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gaudete (Erasure)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2013</span><span class="sg-chain-h">electronic version, first single from Snow Globe</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Crudités (Blanche Rowen and Mike Gulston)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2013</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Potentia Animi, Das erste Gebet</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2004</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody with new words for the verses</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">I'm Alan Partridge</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Steeleye Span's version used in the comedy</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Older liturgical books</span><span class="sg-chain-h">source of the standard tune</span></li></ul></section>
